 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to increasing the rate of taxation of\nthe hotel or motel tax in the county of Schenectady to 5%",
    "basePrintNo": "S5761",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5761-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1202-e, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5761\n\nSPONSOR: AMEDORE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to increasing\nthe rate of taxation of the hotel or motel tax in the county of Schenec-\ntady to 5%\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would allow the hotel/motel tax in Schenectady County to be\nraised from four percent to five percent.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends subdivision 1 of section 1202-e of the Tax Law, last\namended in 2003, to authorize Schenectady County to increase the rate of\ntaxation on persons occupying hotel or motel rooms in the County a rate\nof four percent to a rate of five percent of the per diem rental rate\nfor each room provided.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nCurrent law allows for a four percent tax rate on hotel or motel rooms\nin Schenectady County.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis proposal has been introduced at the request of the Schenectady\nCounty Legislature.\n\nThe revenue generated from the current hotel/motel tax has been used for\nthe betterment of tourism, arts and historic preservation throughout\nSchenectady County. The funds have allowed the County to make signif-\nicant investments in Proctors Theater, fund County special events and\nprovide grants to community arts organizations. Additional funds gener-\nated under the proposal will allow the County to build upon these\nprograms by providing Schenectady with the tools and resources needed to\nnot only ensure the success of the new casino complex, but to highlight\nall of the assets Schenectady County has to offer. The County plans to\noperate a new Tourism and Convention Bureau with funds generated by this\nadditional tax.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017: S.4468/A.6041 - Remained in Senate Investigations & Gov't Oper-\nations Committee; Passed Assembly.\n2018: Remained in Senate Investigations & Gov't Operations Committee;\nRemained on assembly 3rd Reading Calendar.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThe first of the month next succeeding the date on which it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
